ue han pasado por una laringuectomía, ya que la afagia puede complicar significativamente la recuperación y la calidad de vida del paciente [Data: Relationships (16263)].", "# Otolaryngology Community and Laryngeal Carcinoma Treatment\n\nThe community is centered around the Otolaryngology department (ORL) and its involvement in the treatment of a patient diagnosed with carcinoma epidermoide de laringe. Key entities include the ORL, the Comité de Tumores, and various treatment procedures, all of which are interconnected in the patient's care pathway.\n\n## Role of the Otolaryngology Department (ORL)\n\nThe ORL department is pivotal in the evaluation and treatment of the patient with laryngeal carcinoma. It specializes in conditions affecting the ear, nose, and throat, and is directly involved in the patient's treatment and follow-up care. The department's comprehensive approach includes managing dysphagia, which is crucial for patients undergoing treatment for head and neck cancers. The ORL's involvement is essential for ensuring that the patient receives appropriate care tailored to their specific needs, particularly in managing complications related to their condition. [Data: Entities (2892); Relationships (3362, 349, 10719, 10720, 2450, +more)]\n\n## Significance of Carcinoma Epidermoide de Laringe\n\nCarcinoma epidermoide de laringe is a serious condition affecting the patient's larynx, necessitating a comprehensive treatment plan. The patient's diagnosis is complicated by the presence of diabetes mellitus, which may affect treatment outcomes and options. The severity of this cancer type and its implications for the patient's health underscore the importance of timely and effective intervention. The treatment plan includes surgery, chemotherapy, and radiotherapy, highlighting the multifaceted approach required to manage this condition effectively. [Data: Entities (7063); Relationships (1559, 905, 16258, 16259, +more)]\n\n## Function of the Comité de Tumores\n\nTh